meta {
  name: Send Location (with order)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/{{master_id}}/location
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "latitude": 37.983321,
    "longitude": 58.385545,
    "order_id": {{order_id}},
    "recorded_at": "2026-05-16T13:45:00+05:00"
  }
}

docs {
  # Send Live Location

  Call every 10–15 seconds while the master is working. Requires the token —
  the `{master}` segment is kept for URL compatibility, but it must match the
  authenticated master or the request is rejected.

  - `order_id` — optional; set when tied to a specific order trip
  - `recorded_at` — optional ISO8601; defaults to server `now()`

  The client tracking screen reads these pings through `master.location` in
  **Track Order**, and the auto-search uses the latest one to decide which
  orders are within reach — a master who has never pinged sees an empty feed.

  **Response 201:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "id": 1234,
      "master_id": 11,
      "order_id": 1,
      "latitude": 37.952321,
      "longitude": 58.382345,
      "recorded_at": "2026-05-16T13:45:00+05:00"
    }
  }
  ```

  **Errors:**
  - `403` — the id in the URL is not the authenticated master
  - `422` — validation error
}
